      "writtenOn": "2023-08-01T19:38:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the original filter, we didn\u0027t do anything special and just assumed there was a colorspace match (and CFs weren\u0027t a thing). kForceResolveInputs was an aggressive way to do that, kSampledRepeatedly now should allow for transformed-only inputs to avoid an intermediate image.\n\nOn all the multi-passes for really big kernels, the \"input\" is the output of the prior stage and won\u0027t have a CF, or colorspace mismatch so won\u0027t trigger anything extra.",
